# L §4.2 key arithmetic and §7.1 integer offsets: on an integer index, `x - 1` in a key position is the previous key,
# never the literal 1 read as a key.  b[60] = 0 (rule first); b[x] = a[x - 1] = x - 1 for x > 60.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index ages = int 60..63
def a[x in ages]: int = x at reader
def b[x in ages]: int at reader
  rule first = 0
  rule next beats first = a[x - 1] when x > 60

ask q: b[x] for x in ages law 2026-01-01
=== expect
q (x = 60): 0
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-12-31
q (x = 61): 60
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-12-31
q (x = 62): 61
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-12-31
q (x = 63): 62
  law date 2026-01-01, cut 2026-12-31
